</div><div class="programme d-flex">
	<div class="d-flex flex-column details-wrapper">
		<div class="programme-image">
			<img src="" alt="The Yellow Tie" class="image border"/>
		</div>
		<div class="synopsis">
			<p class="MsoNormal">The epic true story of Sergiu Celibidache, following the legendary composer from a childhood spent under his father’s draconian authority, through to adulthood as he masters his craft in Berlin. However, his greatest struggle emerges at the outbreak of war. With the world collapsing around him, Sergiu must evade death and starvation to cement his place in the world of classical music, but risks being torn apart by a relentless pursuit for perfection that could overshadow his legacy forever.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal">Directed by Sergiu's son, Serge Ioan Celibidache, this uniquely personal tale of family, duty and dreams stars a magnificent cast including&nbsp;<b>Ben Schnetzer&nbsp;</b>(<i>The Madison,</i>&nbsp;<i>Pride</i>), Academy Award-nominee&nbsp;<b>John Malkovich&nbsp;</b>(<i>Burn After Reading, Adaptation</i>), BAFTA-winner&nbsp;<b>Sean Bean&nbsp;</b>(<i>Game of Thrones, The Lord of the Rings</i>), Academy Award-nominee&nbsp;<b>Miranda Richardson&nbsp;</b>(<i>Sleepy Hollow, The Hours</i>), and&nbsp;<b>Kate Phillips&nbsp;</b>(<i>Peaky Blinders, Wolf Hall</i>).<span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="d-flex flex-column performance-list-wrapper">		
		<h2 class="title"><a href="https://book.ilkleycinema.co.uk/IlkleyCinema.dll/TSelectItems.waSelectItemsPrompt.TcsWebMenuItem_1030.TcsWebTab_1031.TcsProgramme_12590896">The Yellow Tie</a> / <span class="highlight">SHOWTIMES</span></h2>	
		<div class="performance-list">
			<table cellpadding="0"><tr valign="top"><td><table cellpadding="0"><tr><td class="PeformanceListDate">Tuesday 13 Oct 2026</td><td width="10px"></td><td class="PeformanceListTimes"><span class="StartTimeAndStatus"><a class="Button" href="https://book.ilkleycinema.co.uk/IlkleyCinema.dll/TSelectItems.waSelectItemsPrompt.TcsWebMenuItem_1030.TcsWebTab_1031.TcsPerformance_12595672.TcsSection_596618" title="Click to Book">13:45</a></span></td></tr></table></td></tr></table>
		</div>
	</div>
</div><div class="programme d-flex">
	<div class="d-flex flex-column details-wrapper">
		<div class="programme-image">
			<img src="https://images.savoysystems.co.uk/ICI/12434560.jpeg" alt="National Theatre Live: The Misanthrope" class="image border"/>
		</div>
		<div class="synopsis">
			<div class="films-single__syn-featured"><p>Award-winner Sandra Oh (Killing Eve) plays the title role in this razor-sharp reimagining of Molière’s classic dark comedy.</p><p><br></p></div><div class="films-single__syn"><p>Telling the truth isn’t always that simple. Alice, a brilliant novelist, despises the carefully constructed lies of modern society. But the more she challenges those around her, the fiercer the backlash becomes. Soon, she must confront the price of speaking her truth in a world that would rather silence her.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Filmed live on stage at the National Theatre, Indhu Rubasingham directs Martin Crimp’s (Cyrano de Bergerac) highly anticipated play.</p></div>
		</div>
	</div>
