</div><div class="programme d-flex">
	<div class="d-flex flex-column details-wrapper">
		<div class="programme-image">
			<img src="" alt="Fallen Angels" class="image border"/>
		</div>
		<div class="synopsis">
			<p class="MsoNormal">Sparkling, dizzying, and deliciously potent,&nbsp;<b><i>Fallen Angels</i></b>, Noël Coward’s champagne-fresh comedy of bad manners, shocked and delighted audiences at its 1925 premiere. Two upper-class wives, their husbands away for the day, share a few toasts to their pre-marital dalliances—with the same man, who just may be&nbsp;<i>en route</i>&nbsp;from France to visit. Old rivalries and past scandals bubble to the surface in this intoxicating romp from one of theatre’s comedy masters.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Starring Golden Globe-winner&nbsp;<b>Rose Byrne</b>&nbsp;(<i>If I Had Legs I’d Kick You</i>) and Tony Award winner&nbsp;<b>Kelli O’Hara</b>&nbsp;(<i>The King and I</i>), with&nbsp;<b>Tracee Chimo</b>,&nbsp;<b>Mark Consuelos</b>&nbsp;(making his Broadway debut),&nbsp;<b>Christopher Fitzgerald</b>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<b>Aasif Mandvi</b>, this new Roundabout Theatre and Tony Award-winning production of ‘pure escapist fun’ (<i>The New York Times</i>) was filmed live on stage at Broadway’s Todd Haimes Theatre and now comes to the big screen.<o:p></o:p></p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="d-flex flex-column performance-list-wrapper">		
