</div><div class="programme d-flex">
	<div class="d-flex flex-column details-wrapper">
		<div class="programme-image">
			<img src="" alt="Andrew Lloyd Webber's Starlight Express - Live On Stage" class="image border"/>
		</div>
		<div class="synopsis">
			<p class="x_MsoNormal">Filmed live at the specially designed Starlight Auditorium at Troubadour Wembley Park Theatre,&nbsp;<b>Andrew Lloyd Webber's Starlight Express - Live On Stage</b>&nbsp;will immerse audiences in a world of speed, song and storytelling as an incredible cast of 40 whizz across the screen, performing some of musical theatre’s most beloved songs.</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">As a child’s train set magically comes to life and the engines race to become the fastest in the world, Rusty the steam train has little hope of winning until he is inspired by the legend of the ‘Starlight Express’.</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">A classic stage show, it has been seen around the world by over 30 million people over the last 40 years. With music by Andrew Lloyd Webber and lyrics by Richard Stilgoe,&nbsp;<b>Andrew Lloyd Webber's Starlight Express - Live On Stage</b>&nbsp;is an electrifying experience for all ages, on the big screen for the very first&nbsp;time.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="d-flex flex-column performance-list-wrapper">		
		<h2 class="title"><a href="https://book.ilkleycinema.co.uk/IlkleyCinema.dll/TSelectItems.waSelectItemsPrompt.TcsWebMenuItem_1030.TcsWebTab_1031.TcsProgramme_12659800">Andrew Lloyd Webber's Starlight Express - Live On Stage</a> / <span class="highlight">SHOWTIMES</span></h2>	
		<div class="performance-list">
			<table cellpadding="0"><tr valign="top"><td><table cellpadding="0"><tr><td class="PeformanceListDate">Sunday 6 Dec 2026</td><td width="10px"></td><td class="PeformanceListTimes"><span class="StartTimeAndStatus"><a class="Button" href="https://book.ilkleycinema.co.uk/IlkleyCinema.dll/TSelectItems.waSelectItemsPrompt.TcsWebMenuItem_1030.TcsWebTab_1031.TcsPerformance_12660366.TcsSection_596618" title="Click to Book">14:00</a></span></td></tr></table></td></tr></table>
		</div>
	</div>
</div><div class="programme d-flex">
	<div class="d-flex flex-column details-wrapper">
		<div class="programme-image">
			<img src="" alt="Exhibition on Screen: Renoir &amp; Love" class="image border"/>
		</div>
		<div class="synopsis">
			<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 1rem; text-align: inherit;">Pierre-Auguste Renoir is one of the world’s favourite artists; a founding member of the Impressionist movement and a constantly evolving artist, he is unmatched at depicting human connection. The National Gallery’s blockbuster exhibition brings together vibrant masterpieces which explore love in all its forms, bringing colour and warmth into the cold winter months.</span><span style="font-size: 1rem; text-align: inherit;">&nbsp;</span><br></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">With exclusive access to this exciting new show, Exhibition on Screen will bring these world class works to cinema audiences, with close examination of the art and leading experts exploring the immense skill and influence of this master of colour and connection. Be transported back to a Parisian summer of love through the eyes of a true visionary. An unmissable opportunity to fall in love with Renoir this winter.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal">Made in close collaboration with The National Gallery, London.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal">Directed by Ali Ray </p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
		</div>
	</div>
