</div><div class="programme d-flex">
	<div class="d-flex flex-column details-wrapper">
		<div class="programme-image">
			<img src="" alt="The Royal Ballet: Swan Lake (2027)" class="image border"/>
		</div>
		<div class="synopsis">
			<p class="MsoNormal">The Royal Ballet<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><i>SWAN LAKE<o:p></o:p></i></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b>LIVE:&nbsp;</b>Thursday 22nd April 2027, 19:15 BST&nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b>ENCORE:</b>&nbsp;Sunday 25th April 2027, 14:00 BST<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Approximate runtime: 3h 25min / 205min, Two Intervals&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b>Cast:<o:p></o:p></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></b></p><p class="MsoNormal">To be confirmed<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b>Creatives:&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></b></p><p class="MsoNormal">Choreography MARIUS PETIPA, LEV IVANOV&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Additional Choreography LIAM SCARLETT, FREDERICK ASHTON&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Music PYOTR IL’YICH TCHAIKOVSKY&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Conductor KOEN KESSELS<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Production LIAM SCARLETT&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Designer JOHN MACFARLANE&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Lighting Designer DAVID FINN<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b>Synopsis:&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></b></p><p class="MsoNormal">Princess Odette is bound by a curse, turned into a swan by the evil sorcerer Von Rothbart. The spell can only be broken by a pledge of eternal love. When she meets Prince Siegfried, he is immediately enamoured by her fragile beauty and pledges to free her. But freedom is not promised for Odette as Von Rothbart conspires to thwart the lovers’ plans.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Liam Scarlett’s production for The Royal Ballet brings together Tchaikovsky’s towering score and John Macfarlane’s picturesque designs to create an enduring ballet spectacle of love, treachery and forgiveness.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><br clear="all"><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
